                  Restraint support across energy engines


        CHARMM can evaluate energies through five engines: its own CPU code,
DOMDEC, DOMDEC_GPU, OpenMM and BLaDE.  They do not implement the same
restraints.
A restraint the CPU path honours may be translated by one engine, refused by
another, and quietly left out by a third, so a script that is correct under
one engine can be running different physics under another.

This file records which engine honours which restraint.  It is derived from
the code rather than from the other documentation files, because those were
found to disagree with the code when this survey was made (see *note
Doc drift::).


