                     Restraint support by engine

                                        CPU  DOMDEC  DD_GPU  OpenMM  BLaDE
  ------------------------------------- ---  ------  ------  ------  -----
  CONS HARM absolute                    yes  yes     yes     part    part
  CONS HARM relative/bestfit/RMSD       yes  no      no      no      no
  Principal component harmonic (PCHARM) yes  yes*    yes*    yes     no
  CONS DIHE                             yes  yes     yes     yes     yes
  CONS RESD                             yes  yes     yes     yes!    part
  CONS HMCM                             yes  yes     yes     NO-DYN  no
  NOE distance restraints               yes  yes     yes     NO-DYN  part
  MMFP GEO sphere/cylinder/plane        yes  yes     yes     yes     no
  MMFP GEO COM bond/angle/dihedral      yes  yes     yes     part    yes
  Distance matrix (DMC)                 yes  yes     yes     NO-DYN  no
  RXNCOR umbrella                       yes  yes     yes     NO-DYN  no
  Adaptive umbrella (ADUMB)             yes  yes     yes     NO-DYN  no
  BLOCK CATS                            yes  part    part    NO-DYN  yes
  Shape restraint (SHAP)                yes  no      no      NO-DYN  no
  Puckering restraint (CPUC)            yes  no      no      NO-DYN  no
  Internal coordinate (CIC)             yes  no      no      NO-DYN  no
  Radius of gyration (RGY)              yes  yes     yes     NO-DYN  no
  Pulling force (PULL)                  yes  yes     yes     NO-DYN  no
  Droplet restraint (CDRO)              yes  yes     yes     NO-DYN  no
  Solvent boundary (SBOU)               yes  yes*    yes*    NO-DYN  no
  Dipole MMFP (MDIP)                    yes  yes     yes     NO-DYN  no

  yes     evaluated, and it acts on the dynamics
  no      not evaluated; see *note Reporting:: for whether you are told
  part    some cases only; see that engine's section
  NO-DYN  an ENERgy call reports it, but it does not act during dynamics
          through that engine.  See below -- this is the dangerous one.
  yes*    structurally the same as the rows around it, but not measured
  yes!    measured working, with one reproducible crash: see *note OpenMM::

DD_GPU is DOMDEC_GPU.  Its column is identical to DOMDEC's, and that is
structural rather than coincidence: the restraint block in
source/energy/energy.F90 sits after the q_gpu branch, which only reorders
the bonded and nonbonded work, and every restraint guard tests q_domdec,
which q_gpu implies.  A restraint added to one is added to both.

                   Why NO-DYN and not simply "no"

Everything in this table was measured, not inferred, with
tool/restraint_matrix.  The measurement that matters is not whether the
engine reports the right energy.  It is whether the restraint acts.

For an ENERgy evaluation, CHARMM still computes the restraints OpenMM does
not implement, and they appear in the reported total.  Nothing looks wrong.
But dynamics through OpenMM is integrated inside OpenMM, using only the
forces in the OpenMM System, and a restraint CHARMM computed on its own is
not in there.

Measured: DHFR in a cubic box, PULL force 500 on the CA atoms all in +x,
200 steps of leapfrog dynamics from the same coordinates.

  CPU      CA centroid moved  +0.633 Angstrom in x
  OpenMM   CA centroid moved  -0.0008 Angstrom -- it did not move

The restraint was reported by ENERgy in both cases.  It acted in one.

So an energy comparison is not a test of restraint support for OpenMM, and
a script that checks its restraint energy looks correct while running
unrestrained dynamics.

Two rows to read carefully:

  - MMFP GEO is marked supported for both OpenMM and BLaDE, but the two
    take disjoint parts of it.  OpenMM takes the geometric forms (sphere,
    cylinder, plane); BLaDE refuses those and takes only the centre-of-mass
    bond, angle and dihedral forms.  There is no MMFP GEO script that runs
    the same way on both.

  - BLaDE's whole column is unmeasured: it needs a CUDA build, which the
    machine this survey was run on does not have.  It is read from the
    code.  Run tool/restraint_matrix where a BLaDE build exists.

